  "solutions": [
    {
      "id": "sol.amc-8-2015-p6.live",
      "kind": "proof-sketch",
      "text": "Drop the altitude from \\(B\\) to \\(AC,\\) meeting \\(AC\\) at \\(X.\\) Since \\(AB=BC,\\) point \\(X\\) is the midpoint of \\(AC,\\) so \\(AX=21.\\)\n\nIn right triangle \\(ABX,\\) the altitude is \\[ \\begin{aligned} BX &= \\sqrt{29^2-21^2} \\\\ &= \\sqrt{400} = 20. \\end{aligned} \\]\n\nThe area of \\(\\triangle ABC\\) is \\(\\dfrac12\\cdot42\\cdot20=420.\\)\n\nThus, B is the correct answer.",
      "hints": [
        "Drop the altitude from \\(B\\) to \\(AC.\\)",
        "The altitude bisects \\(AC,\\) giving a right triangle with hypotenuse \\(29.\\)"
      ],
      "images": []
